<title>USA: Leslie Building Products Q4 shr loss down.</title>
<headline>Leslie Building Products Q4 shr loss down.</headline>
<dateline>WHITE PLAINS, N.Y. 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year Ended	    Quarter Ended</p>
<p>				   December 31,	  December 31,</p>
<p>(In thousands, except</p>
<p> per share amounts)	   1996	1995	1996     1995</p>
<p> Net sales		    $82,154  $75,993   $16,208  $15,299</p>
<p>Facilities restructuring</p>
<p>  charge(a)				  2,816		  1,962</p>
<p> Revaluation of goodwill(b)	    5,092</p>
<p>    Subtotal		   13,199   20,453     3,027    4,862</p>
<p>    Operating profit(loss)  2,299  (6,970)     (225)  (2,192)</p>
<p> Interest expense, net	1,672    1,099	 399	339</p>
<p>    Net income(loss)(c)	 627  (8,069)     (624)  (2,531)</p>
<p>Net income (loss)</p>
<p>     per common share	   .13   (1.68)     (.13)    (.53)</p>
<p>NOTE - (a) Represents a charge for the cost to restructure the company's manufacturing facilities in order to achieve more efficient and less costly manufacturing and distribution of products.</p>
<p>(b) During 1995, the company reevaluated its accounting policy towards measurement of goodwill and changed to a fair value method. Based upon a valuation by an independent business appraiser, of Leslie-Locke Inc, the company's sole operating subsidiary, it was determined that the goodwill previously reflected on the company's financial statements had no value. Accordingly, the company wrote off the balance of goodwill of $5,092,000 as of August 31, 1995. Goodwill amortization had been $170,000 per annum.</p>
</text>
